---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Design Ideas for v6';
const date = '2020-01-05';
const category = 'Development';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} - Dasher Blog`}>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <article class="blog-post">
      <header class="blog-header">
        <div class="blog-meta">
          <time datetime={date}>
            {new Date(date).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
              year: 'numeric',
              month: 'long',
              day: 'numeric',
            })}
          </time>
          <span class="blog-tag">{category}</span>
        </div>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="blog-content">
        <p>
          As we begin work on Dasher v6, we're exploring various design concepts and ideas that
          could improve the user experience and expand Dasher's capabilities.
        </p>

        <h2>Core Principles</h2>
        <p>
          Dasher v6 will maintain the core principles that have made Dasher successful:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Information Efficiency</strong> - Optimizing for maximum information throughput</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility First</strong> - Ensuring Dasher works for users with diverse needs</li>
          <li><strong>Adaptability</strong> - Learning from user behavior to improve predictions</li>
          <li><strong>Simplicity</strong> - Maintaining an intuitive interface</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Potential Improvements</h2>
        <p>
          Some areas we're exploring for v6 include:
        </p>

        <h3>Visual Design</h3>
        <p>
          While Dasher's visual design is iconic, there may be opportunities to make it more
          approachable for new users while retaining its core visual metaphor. We're considering
          color schemes, contrast options, and visual feedback improvements.
        </p>

        <h3>Language Model Integration</h3>
        <p>
          Modern language models have advanced significantly since Dasher's original design. We're
          exploring how to integrate these improvements while maintaining Dasher's efficiency and
          privacy focus.
        </p>

        <h3>Input Method Expansion</h3>
        <p>
          Dasher has always been flexible in terms of input methods. For v6, we're looking at:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Better eye-tracking integration</li>
          <li>Improved touch/stylus support</li>
          <li>Voice-assisted navigation</li>
          <li>Brain-computer interface research</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Platform Support</h3>
        <p>
          Modern development tools make cross-platform development easier. We're prioritizing:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Web-based Dasher for browser access</li>
          <li>Improved mobile experience</li>
          <li>Better support for assistive technology integration</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Community Input</h2>
        <p>
          These are just some of the ideas we're considering. We want to hear from the community
          about what's most important to you. What would make Dasher more useful for you or those
          you support?
        </p>
        <p>
          Join the discussion on <a href="https://matrix.to/#/#dasher:matrix.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Matrix</a>
          or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/dasher-project/dasher" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          with your ideas and feedback.
        </p>
      </div>

      <footer class="blog-footer">
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn-secondary">← Back to Blog</a>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .blog-post {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0;
  }

  .blog-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .blog-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .blog-tag {
    background-color: var(--color-horizon-mint);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .blog-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .blog-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-horizon-mint);
  }

  .blog-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .blog-content ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .blog-content li {
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    position: relative;
  }

  .blog-content li::before {
    content: '•';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-target-coral);
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .blog-content strong {
    color: var(--color-deep-ink);
  }

  .blog-footer {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-horizon-mint);
  }
</style>
